title: "The Peacekeepers' Arms Race: Testing the Stability-Instability Paradox in Cross-National Conflict Data, 1946-2024"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Davis"
    given-names: "T Sam"
repository-code: "https://github.com/plutorion275/peacekeepers-arms-race"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21947818
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21947819
    description: "Archived snapshot of version v1.0.0, the version this identifier covers. The record's concept DOI (10.5281/zenodo.21947818) always resolves to the latest version."
version: v1.0.1
abstract: >-
  A quantitative panel-data study testing the Stability-Instability
  Paradox across 192 countries (1946-2024): whether higher military
  capability shifts conflict composition toward low-intensity forms
  (substitution) or amplifies all conflict types (amplification).
  Combines panel fixed-effects regression, Dumitrescu-Hurlin panel
  Granger causality, and K-Means clustering on SIPRI, UCDP, World
  Bank, V-Dem, and Correlates of War data.
keywords:
  - stability-instability paradox
  - panel data
  - Granger causality
  - conflict studies
  - military expenditure
  - clustering
